# If the offsets are stale, use `patch --fuzz 3` or apply the hunks manually.
# The semantic intent of each hunk is described in comments above it.
#
# What this patch does:
#   1. Adds CAPTURE_MODE (AtomicBool) and CAPTURE_SLOT (Mutex<Option<Crate>>)
#      module-level statics to json/mod.rs.
#   2. In JsonRenderer::after_krate, after assembling the `types::Crate` value
#      but BEFORE writing to disk: if CAPTURE_MODE is true, store the value into
#      CAPTURE_SLOT and return early (skipping the BufWriter/serde_json::to_writer).
#   3. Exposes `pub fn capture_crate(at_args: Vec<String>) -> Result<Vec<u8>, ...>`
#      which sets the capture mode, drives run_from_commandline, and returns the
#      assembled JSON bytes from memory — never touching the filesystem.
#
# The driver (workspace/rustdoc-driver/driver/src/main.rs) calls capture_crate
# and immediately lowers the returned bytes via serde_json → rustdoc_types::Crate
# → RustdocParser. No JSON file is ever written to or read from disk.

